{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Implementation notes (verification of the certified plan against the tree, at origin/main).\n\nEvery factual claim in the plan held. Only line numbers had drifted by ~2 (the plan's\n`docs/plan-review-gate.md:1325` for `## R4` is 1327; `486-489` is 486-490); the AC commands are\nall `awk`-range based, so none of them depended on those numbers. Verified before implementing:\n- `SKILL.md` Step 7 is two independent axes with independent triggers, and already mandates\n  RED->GREEN per sibling with ticket-filing as the out-of-scope fallback — as the plan states.\n- `SKILL.md:564` (Phase 1 exit gate) does already say declare `file_impact` + `rebar review-plan`\n  for a non-trivial fix, so Step 7 links to it rather than restating it.\n- `orchestrator.bug_blast_radius_escalates` exists at `orchestrator.py:191`, consumed at\n  `orchestrator.py:245` and `workflow_ops.py:127`, and the classification rule (\"test\" iff under\n  `tests/` or basename `conftest.py`) matches `code_review/bugfix_size_gate.py:97`.\n- The two contradicting docs passages exist verbatim and did contradict the shipped escalation.\n\nTwo corrections made beyond the plan, both to keep the written text true:\n1. The plan's illustrative `rebar set-file-impact <bug> <path>...` is not the real signature —\n   `rebar set-file-impact --help` takes a JSON array of `{path,reason}` objects. Step 7 now shows\n   the real form.\n2. The existing docs sentence \"downgrades every DET finding to advisory (`det_blocking:[]`)\" is\n   itself inaccurate: `workflow_ops.plan_review_precheck` preserves P4's description-admission\n   block and downgrades the rest. Since that sentence was being rewritten anyway for the\n   escalation exception, it is now correct on both counts.\n\nAC deviation: AC#8 asserts `git diff --name-only origin/main` lists only the two documentation\nfiles. The change also adds `tests/unit/test_rebar_debug_step7_class_review.py`, the contract test\nfor the new directive (the epic's tests-first discipline). That is the change's own test, not a\ncollateral edit; no other file is touched.\n\nMutation evidence — each of the 9 assertions was killed by a targeted perturbation of the\ndocumentation it governs, then restored:\n- `review-plan` name mangled in Step 7 -> routes-through-plan-review RED.\n- `set-file-impact` name mangled -> file-impact RED (and portability RED).\n- \"acceptance criterion\" -> \"AC\" -> acceptance-criterion RED.\n- \"the Phase 1 exit gate\" -> \"the earlier exit gate\" -> cross-reference RED.\n- Step 7's link replaced by a second copy of the blast-radius rationale -> non-duplication RED.\n- tracker conditioning dropped (\"When the project's tracker is rebar\" -> \"When the project uses\"),\n  and separately the generic-equivalent half dropped -> portability RED for each half\n  independently. (The first version of this assertion scoped the block too widely and survived\n  the mutation by picking up \"tracker\" from a neighbouring list item; it is now scoped to the\n  numbered step and requires both halves.)\n- `bug_blast_radius_escalates` removed from R4 -> R4-documents-escalation RED.\n- Each never-blocks qualifier reverted independently -> the corresponding parametrised case RED."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787377010744969001,"uuid":"7ab0a74d-a0a3-49fb-ac90-2f417aff18a3"}